<title>RUSSIA: Russia sets 47.09 pct in bond coupon payment.</title>
<headline>Russia sets 47.09 pct in bond coupon payment.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1996-10-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Russia's finance ministry set a 47.09 percent annual rate for the fourth quarterly coupon to be paid on the two-year OFZ government bond (series 24006) maturing in February 1998, the central bank said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>The coupon date is February 5, 1997, and the interest amounts to 117,402 roubles.</p>
<p>The third coupon, to be paid on November 6, amounts to 68.05 percent annual, or 169,659 roubles.</p>
<p>--Anna Smirnova, Moscow Newsroom, +7095 941 8520</p>
</text>
